% @MCCODE_PREFIX@rtdiff(1)
% @FLAVOR_UPPER@ @MCCODE_PARTICLE@ Ray Tracing Team
% @MCCODE_DATE@

# NAME

**@MCCODE_PREFIX@rtdiff** - Compare per-instrument execution times across
multiple runs/builds of the @MCCODE_PREFIX@test tool

# SYNOPSIS

**@MCCODE_PREFIX@rtdiff** [-h] [--reflabel REFLABEL] [--metric {runtime,compiletime,displaytime}] [--output OUTPUT] [--title TITLE] [--top TOP] [--nobrowse] [INPUT ...]

# DESCRIPTION

The tool **@MCCODE_PREFIX@rtdiff** reads the
`testresults_<label>.json` files written out by **@MCCODE_PREFIX@test**
(one per build/run) and compares the per-instrument timing values. It
produces a total-runtime summary comparing builds and a per-instrument
comparison showing absolute and relative differences against a chosen
reference build, rendered both as a console table and as a
self-contained HTML report (standard library only, no external
dependencies).

Each mctest run writes, inside its label directory:

    <testdir>/<label>/testresults_<label>.json

The JSON is a dictionary keyed by instrument display name plus a
`_meta` key holding run metadata. Each instrument entry contains the
timing fields **@MCCODE_PREFIX@rtdiff** compares:

- `runtime` - seconds for the %Example test run (default metric)
- `compiletime` - seconds spent compiling the instrument
- `displaytime` - seconds for the mcdisplay run

Values that are null, non-numeric, negative, or absent are treated as
"no data" and shown as `n/a`; they are excluded from totals and
differences and are never treated as zero.

# OPTIONS

**-h, --help**
:   show this help message and exit

**--reflabel REFLABEL**
:   Reference build label for comparison. If unset, the oldest build
    (by file modification time) is used.

**--metric {runtime,compiletime,displaytime}**
:   Which timing field to compare (default: `runtime`).

**--output OUTPUT**
:   Output HTML file (default: `./mcrtdiff_report.html`).

**--title TITLE**
:   Title for the generated report.

**--top TOP**
:   Show only the top-N most-changed instruments in the console table
    (the HTML report always shows all).

**--nobrowse**
:   Do not open the generated report in a browser on exit.

**INPUT ...**
:   One or more inputs: a testdir root containing one subfolder per
    build (the mctest layout), a single label directory holding a
    `testresults_*.json` file, or a direct path to a
    `testresults_*.json` file. The current directory is used if
    omitted.

# EXAMPLES

Compare every build found inside an mctest results folder:
:   `@MCCODE_PREFIX@rtdiff /path/to/mctest-results`

Compare two specific label directories, using the first as reference:
:   `@MCCODE_PREFIX@rtdiff --reflabel build-a build-a build-b`

Compare compile times instead of run times:
:   `@MCCODE_PREFIX@rtdiff --metric compiletime /path/to/mctest-results`

# FILES

/usr/share/@FLAVOR@/tools/Python/@MCCODE_PREFIX@test/@MCCODE_PREFIX@rtdiff.py

